# ROUND 1 EVIDENCE BRIEF — Archaeoacoustics canon vs. contested claims
Prepared for the crop-circle cymatics / ancient-monument acoustic cross-domain matching study.

⚠️ **Two citation errors in the consultation prompt, corrected below:**
- Watson & Keating 1999 is in **Antiquity 73(280): 325–336**, *not* World Archaeology 31 — and it did not measure Stonehenge; it measured a recumbent stone circle and a passage-grave **in Scotland**.
- The 2020 Stonehenge scale-model paper is Cox, Fazenda & Greaney in **Journal of Archaeological Science 122: 105218**, *not* JASA. (Fazenda & Drumm's 2013 paper is in *Acta Acustica united with Acustica* 99(1): 110–117.)

